  it's the idea of dinamis  of potentiality  democracy is ever changing it is a  promise that must constantly be  fulfilled  and that is what makes it stand out from  autocracy  democracy may be not perfect  but it is perfectable  so take Ukraine  when we granted Ukraine the status of  candidate to joining our Union  some objected that ukrainians democracy  may still be too young  but since the maidan protest of 2014  Ukraine's democracy has grown so much  in a few years it has reformed more than  in previous decades  it has set up anti-corruption  institutions  it has adopted first laws  to break the oligarchs grip on Ukraine's  economic political and public life  its Civil Society has conquered new  space  and holds the government to account  and the country's institutions are now  passing the ultimate stress test of work  most of this progress has been achieved  because the people of Ukraine have  Europe in their hearts and in their  minds  and the same is true for our friends in  Albania in North Macedonia and Across  the Western Balkan it is true for  Moldova and Georgia who have also asked  to join our Union  once again  the Wind of Change is blowing across our  continent  ladies and gentlemen  all democracies are constant work in  progress  including inside our Union  the European Union was built on the  promise Unity  in diversity  but this promise has yet to be achieved  in full  the path towards full equality for all  citizens is still law  racism  and anti-Semitism have not disappeared  and in parts of our Union minorities are  not always respected  lgbtiq rights continue to be violated  the rule of law and the independence of  the Judiciary are still challenged  we have seen judges stripped of the  immunity  and driven out of office without  justification  and serious concerns have been raised on  corruption  these developments are against our  values  against our treaties and against our  democracy  and as guardian of the treaty  it is the commission's 